hadiths[53]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19312","Yahya, he is Ibn Said, narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Firas from Mudrik ibn Umarah from Ibn Abi Awfa from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: He does not drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer, nor does he commit adultery when he commits it while he is a believer, nor does he plunder a plunder of honor or excess while he is a believer."
"19313","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: al-Shaybani narrated to me from Ibn Abi Awfa, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan from al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the nabidh of the green jar. He said: I said: And the white? He said: I do not know."
"19314","Waki narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Ubayd ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he raised his head from bowing, said: Allah hears whoever praises Him; O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything after."
"19315","Waki narrated to us: Misar narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Hasan narrated to us from Ibn Abi Awfa that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say that, and he did not say: in the prayer."
"19316","Waki narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us: al-Shaybani narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the nabidh of the green jar. He said: I said: And the white? He said: I do not know."
"19317","Waki and Yala, he is Ibn Ubayd, said: Ibn Abi Khalid, and he is Ismail, narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against the Confederates and said: O Allah, Revealer of the Book, Swift in Reckoning, defeat the Confederates, defeat them and shake them."
"19318","Waki narrated to us from Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa say: We arrived with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he circumambulated the House and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, meaning in the Umrah, while we shielded him from the polytheists lest they harm him with anything."
"19319","Waki narrated to us: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: If there were to be a prophet after the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his son Ibrahim would not have died."
"19320","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Yazid Abu Khalid al-Dalani from Ibrahim al-Saksaki from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot take anything of the Quran, so teach me what will suffice me. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for Allah, mighty and majestic is He, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me and grant me well-being and guide me and provide for me. Then he turned away holding his two palms together, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for this one, he has filled his hands with good. Misar said: And I heard this hadith from Ibrahim al-Saksaki from Ibn Abi Awfa from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and another confirmed it to me."
"19321","Waki narrated to us from Shubah from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: When a man brought the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the charity of his wealth, he would supplicate for him; so I brought him the charity of my father's wealth, and he said: O Allah, bless the family of Abu Awfa."
"19322","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Yafur al-Abdi, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: We went on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seven expeditions, and we used to eat locusts in them."
"19323","Abd al-Rahman, he is Ibn Mahdi, narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from an elder from Bajilah, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: Abu Bakr, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, sought permission upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while with him was a slave-girl beating the tambourine, then Umar, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, sought permission and entered, then Uthman, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, sought permission, and she stopped. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Uthman is a modest man."
"19324","Ismail, he is Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I heard an elder in Madinah narrating that Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa wrote to Ubaydullah when he intended to raid the Haruriyyah, so I said to his scribe, and he was a friend of mine: Copy it for me, so he did: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah, mighty and majestic is He, for well-being; and when you meet them, be patient, and know that Paradise is under the shades of the swords. He said: And he would look, and when the sun declined he would advance upon his enemy, then he said: O Allah, Revealer of the Book, Mover of the clouds, Defeater of the Confederates, defeat them and grant us victory over them."
"19325","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, and he was among the companions of the Tree, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when charity was brought to him, said: O Allah, bless them; and my father brought him his charity, so he said: O Allah, bless the family of Abu Awfa."
"19326","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz said: Shubah narrated to us from Adi, Bahz said: Adi ibn Thabit informed me, Ibn Jafar said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib and Ibn Abi Awfa, they said: They got hold of donkeys on the day of Khaybar, so the caller of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called out to overturn the pots; and Bahz said: from Adi from al-Bara and Ibn Abi Awfa."
"19327","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: a man from Bajilah informed me, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa say: There was a slave-girl beating the tambourine with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then Abu Bakr came, then Umar came, then Uthman, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, came, and she stopped. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Uthman is a modest man."
"19328","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Majzaah ibn Zahir, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me from Majzaah ibn Zahir, and Rawh, they said: Shubah narrated to us from Majzaah ibn Zahir, a freedman of Quraysh, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to say: O Allah, to You is praise, filling the heaven and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything after; O Allah, purify me with snow and hail and cold water; O Allah, purify me of sins and cleanse me of them as the white garment is cleansed of dirt."
"19329","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj from Shubah, he said: I heard Ubayd Abu al-Hasan, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heaven and filling the earth; Hajjaj said: filling the heaven and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything after."
"19330","Muhammad said: Shubah said: And Abu Ismah narrated to me from Sulayman al-Amash from Ubayd from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate when he raised his head from bowing."
"19331","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Overturn the pots and what is in them. Shubah said: Either Sulayman said it, and what is in them, or one who heard it from Ibn Abi Awfa informed me."
"19332","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to me from Abu al-Mukhtar, from Banu Asad, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa say: We were on a journey and did not find water. He said: Then we came upon water after that. He said: And they began to give the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to drink, and whenever they brought him the drink, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupbearer of the people is the last of them, three times, until they all drank."
"19333","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi al-Mujalid say: Abdillah ibn Shaddad and Abu Burdah differed concerning advance payment, so they sent me to Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, and I asked him, so he said: We used to pay in advance in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, for wheat and barley and raisins, or dates, he doubted concerning dates and raisins, and it was not in their possession, or what we did not see in their possession. Then I came to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, and he said the like of that."
"19334","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, said: Talhah informed me, he said: I said to Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bequeath? He said: No. I said: Then how did he command the believers with the bequest when he did not bequeath? He said: He bequeathed the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic is He."
"19335","Hushaym narrated to us: al-Shaybani informed us from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, he said: The people of the mosque sent me to Ibn Abi Awfa to ask him what the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did with the food of Khaybar, so I came to him and asked him about that. He said, and I said: Did he divide it in fifths? He said: No, it was less than that. He said: And when one of us wanted something of it, he would take of it what he needed."
"19336","Hushaym narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, he said: I said to Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, the companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enter the House in his Umrah? He said: No."
"19337","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani informed me, he said: I said to Ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stone? He said: Yes, a Jew and a Jewess. He said: I said: After the revelation of al-Nur or before it? He said: I do not know."
"19338","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Abu Ishaq, meaning al-Shaybani, narrated to us from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade eating the meat of domestic donkeys."
"19339","Ibn Numayr and Yala, the meaning, said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: I said to Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, give glad tidings to Khadijah, may Allah Most High be pleased with her? He said: Yes, he gave her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow reed in which there is no clamor and no toil. Yala said, and he said once: in which there is no clamor, or no idle talk, and no toil."
"19340","Yala narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa say: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he performed Umrah, so he circumambulated and we circumambulated with him, and he prayed and we prayed with him, and he ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and we used to shield him from the people of Makkah lest anyone strike him with anything."
"19341","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Khawarij are the dogs of the Fire."
"19342","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Ismail informed us from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Umrah, so he circumambulated the House and we circumambulated with him, and he prayed behind the Maqam and we prayed with him, then he went out and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, while we were with him shielding him from the people of Makkah lest anyone shoot at him or anyone strike him with anything."
"19343","He said: And he supplicated against the Confederates and said: O Allah, Revealer of the Book, Swift in Reckoning, Defeater of the Confederates, O Allah, defeat them and shake them."
"19344","He said: And I saw on his forearm a wound of a blow, so I said: What is this? He said: I was struck it on the day of Hunayn. So I said to him: Did you witness Hunayn with him? He said: Yes, and before that."
"19345","Yazid narrated to us: Misar informed us from Ziyad ibn Fayyad from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: O Allah, to You is praise, abundant, good, blessed therein."
"19346","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, and he was among the companions of the Tree, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a people brought him charity, said: O Allah, bless them; so my father brought him charity, and he said: O Allah, bless the family of Abu Awfa."
"19347","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us: Iyad narrated to us from Abdillah ibn Said from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: A man came while we were in the row behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and entered the row and said: Allah is Greatest, Most Great, and glory be to Allah morning and evening. He said: So the Muslims raised their heads and disapproved of the man, and said: Who is it that raises his voice above the voice of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, he said: Who is this loud-voiced one? So it was said: Here he is, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: By Allah, I saw your speech ascending into the heaven until a door was opened and it entered into it."
"19348","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Jafar ibn Humayd al-Kufi narrated it to us: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us from Iyad from Abdillah ibn Said from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, the like of it."
"19349","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, narrated to me from Talhah ibn Musarrif, he said: I asked Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bequeath? He said: No. I said: Then why has the bequest been prescribed for the Muslims, or why were they commanded with the bequest? He said: He bequeathed the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic is He."
"19350","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Misar narrated to us from Ubayd ibn Hasan from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything after."
"19351","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Misar narrated to us from Ibrahim al-Saksaki from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I cannot take anything of the Quran, so teach me something that will suffice me of the Quran. He said: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah. He said: And he went away, or stood, or the like of that. He said: This is for Allah, mighty and majestic is He, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me and grant me well-being and guide me and provide for me, or: provide for me and guide me and grant me well-being. Misar said: And perhaps he said: I asked for some of it to be read out to me by Abu Khalid, meaning al-Dalani."
"19352","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Misar narrated to us from Ubayd ibn Hasan, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, to You is praise, filling the heaven and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything after."
"19353","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Ibrahim al-Hajari from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, and he was among the companions of the Tree: a daughter of his died, and he followed her funeral on a mule behind it, and the women began to weep, so he said: Do not recite elegies, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade elegies; then let each of you shed of her tears what she wills. Then he pronounced four takbirs over her, then stood after the fourth for the span between two takbirs, supplicating. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do in the funeral like this."
"19354","al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdillah Abu Abd al-Rahman said, and I heard it myself from al-Hakam, he said: Ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqbah from Abu al-Nadr from Ubaydullah ibn Mamar from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, liked to advance upon his enemy at the declining of the sun."
"19355","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the green jar. He said: I said: The white? He said: I do not know."
"19356","Abdillah narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman, the companion of al-Harawi, whose name is Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad, narrated to me: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave glad tidings to Khadijah of a house in Paradise of hollow reed in which there is no clamor and no toil."
"19357","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Sulayman al-Shaybani from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding the green jar, meaning the nabidh in the green jar. He said: I said: And the white? He said: I do not know."
"19358","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, he said: I said to Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, give glad tidings to Khadijah? He said: Yes, of a house of hollow reed in which there is no clamor and no toil."
"19359","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us from a man from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to stand in the first rakah of the noon prayer until no footfall could be heard."
"19360","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard al-Bara and Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa that they got hold of donkeys and cooked them. He said: So the caller of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called out: Overturn the pots."
"19361","Affan narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us: Iyad narrated to us from Abdillah ibn Said from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: A distant man came, meaning far, while we were in the row behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and entered the row, then said: Allah is Greatest, Most Great, and glory be to Allah morning and evening. So the Muslims raised their heads and disapproved of the man, and said: Who is it that raises his voice above the voice of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, he said: Who is this loud-voiced one? He said: Here he is, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By Allah, I saw your speech ascending into the heaven until a door of it was opened and it entered into it."
"19362","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Said ibn Jumhan narrated to me, he said: We were fighting the Khawarij, and among us was Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, and a youth of his had joined the Khawarij, they being on that bank and we on this bank, so we called to him: Abu Fayruz, Abu Fayruz, woe to you, this is your master Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa. He said: A fine man he is, if only he would emigrate. He said: What does the enemy of Allah say? He said: We said: He says: A fine man, if only he would emigrate. He said: So he said: What emigration after my emigration with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Glad tidings to whoever kills them and is killed by them."
"19363","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abu Yafur, he said: My partner asked, while I was with him, Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa about locusts, so he said: There is no harm in it. And he said: I went on expedition with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seven expeditions, and we used to eat it."
"19364","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I mentioned to Abdillah a hadith narrated to me by Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa concerning donkey meat, so Said said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it decisively."
